meta {
  name: 06 List Reference Range Candidates
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/reference-range/candidates?resultParamId={{resultParamId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  resultParamId: {{resultParamId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  List every `LabTestReferenceRange` row for a Quantitative result parameter
  that matches this report's patient (gender/age) — powers the Test Entry /
  Patient Entry "Range" dropdown, which needs every candidate to choose from
  (unlike Resolve Reference Range, which auto-picks one best match filtered
  by the currently-selected Methodology).

  Covers ranges both with and without an analyzer (`labAdapterId` set or
  null). Quantitative-only: `LabTestReferenceValue`
  (Semi-Quantitative/Qualitative) has no analyzer field, so it always returns
  `{ candidates: [] }` for those param types.

  Returns:
  ```
  {
    candidates: [
      {
        id, labAdapterId, labAdapterName,
        method, unit, isDefault, lowerLimit, upperLimit, referenceDisplay
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Picking a candidate in the dropdown should set Unit/Method/Range together
  (apply the picked row's own fields client-side), then re-submit via Upsert
  Result Values same as Sync.

  404 `LAB_TEST_CATALOGUE_MISSING` if the report has no linked LabTest.
}
